<ontology/use_paper_making/use_paper_making__1015__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 359" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n359> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Glue Size and Gelatine used in Paper Making & Cardboard: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 359"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "SIZE: a liquid glue, made by boiling down in water the clippings of parchment, glove-leather, fish-skin, and other kinds of skin and membrane. It is used in paper-making, by bookbinders, paper-hangers, whitewashers, and painters in distemper."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
